{"9fte":[{"doi":null,"title":"Cryo-EM structure of the adhesion GPCR ADGRV1 in complex with a nanobody","pubmed_id":null,"type":"U","associated_entries":null,"journal_info":{"pdb_abbreviation":"To be published","ISO_abbreviation":null,"pages":"-","volume":null,"issue":null,"year":null},"abstract":{"background":null,"objective":null,"methods":null,"results":null,"conclusions":null,"unassigned":null},"author_list":[{"full_name":"Achat, Y.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Prevost, M.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Mechaly, A.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Genera, M.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Colcombet, J.B.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Bezault, A.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Winter, J.M.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Ayme, G.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Venien-Bryan, C.","last_name":null,"initials":null},{"full_name":"Wolff, N.","last_name":null,"initials":null}]},{"doi":"10.1107/S2059798318006551","title":"Real-space refinement in PHENIX for cryo-EM and crystallography.","pubmed_id":"29872004","type":"J","associated_entries":null,"journal_info":{"pdb_abbreviation":"Acta Crystallogr D Struct Biol","ISO_abbreviation":"Acta Crystallogr D Struct Biol","pages":"531-544","volume":"74","issue":"Pt 6","year":2018},"abstract":{"background":null,"objective":null,"methods":null,"results":null,"conclusions":null,"unassigned":"This article describes the implementation of real-space refinement in the phenix.real_space_refine program from the PHENIX suite. The use of a simplified refinement target function enables very fast calculation, which in turn makes it possible to identify optimal data-restraint weights as part of routine refinements with little runtime cost. Refinement of atomic models against low-resolution data benefits from the inclusion of as much additional information as is available. In addition to standard restraints on covalent geometry, phenix.real_space_refine makes use of extra information such as secondary-structure and rotamer-specific restraints, as well as restraints or constraints on internal molecular symmetry. The re-refinement of 385 cryo-EM-derived models available in the Protein Data Bank at resolutions of 6 Å or better shows significant improvement of the models and of the fit of these models to the target maps."},"author_list":[{"full_name":"Afonine PV","last_name":"Afonine","initials":"PV"},{"full_name":"Poon BK","last_name":"Poon","initials":"BK"},{"full_name":"Read RJ","last_name":"Read","initials":"RJ"},{"full_name":"Sobolev OV","last_name":"Sobolev","initials":"OV"},{"full_name":"Terwilliger TC","last_name":"Terwilliger","initials":"TC"},{"full_name":"Urzhumtsev A","last_name":"Urzhumtsev","initials":"A"},{"full_name":"Adams PD","last_name":"Adams","initials":"PD"}]}]}